<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main>
    <h1>WELCOME TO THE HOME PAGE</h1>
    <p class="home">
        Over the past several weeks, this application has been developed to demonstrate key server-side development concepts.
        The project follows an MVC (Model-View-Controller) architecture. The <strong>Model</strong> manages the data and database interactions,
        the <strong>View</strong> is responsible for presenting information to the user through dynamic pages, and the <strong>Controller</strong>
        handles the application logic and connects user requests to the appropriate models and views.
        <br><br>
        This application also implements <strong>authentication</strong> and <strong>authorization</strong>. Authentication verifies a user’s identity
        (logging in), while authorization determines what actions or areas a user is allowed to access based on their role.
        <br><br>
        A structured PostgreSQL database is used to store and manage application data, demonstrating how server-side programming interacts with
        persistent data through queries and models.
        <br><br>
        In addition, <strong>middleware</strong> is used to enhance security and functionality by handling tasks such as session management,
        request processing, and protecting routes.
        <br><br>
        Please explore the website and enjoy reviewing the features and concepts that have been implemented.
    </p>
</main>
